## 4. Alignment System — Required Distinctions

Alignment is a first-class section, not a single Text Align control.

### 4.1 Text Alignment

| UI control | CSS mapping | Values |
|---|---|---|
| Text Align | `text-align` | start, end, left, right, center, justify |
| Text Align Last | `text-align-last` | auto, start, end, left, right, center, justify |
| Vertical Align | `vertical-align` | baseline, sub, super, text-top, text-bottom, middle, top, bottom, length |
| Direction | `direction` | ltr, rtl |
| Writing Mode | `writing-mode` | horizontal-tb, vertical-rl, vertical-lr |

Show advanced text-flow controls only where applicable.

### 4.2 Flex Container Content Alignment

| UI control | CSS mapping | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Direction | `flex-direction` | Main-axis direction |
| Wrap | `flex-wrap` | Single/multiple flex lines |
| Justify Content | `justify-content` | Distribution on main axis |
| Align Items | `align-items` | Default cross-axis alignment for children |
| Align Content | `align-content` | Distribution of multiple flex lines |
| Gap | `gap` | Space between rows/columns |
| Row Gap | `row-gap` | Vertical line spacing |
| Column Gap | `column-gap` | Horizontal item spacing |

Required values:
- `justify-content`: normal, start, end, flex-start, flex-end, center, left, right, space-between, space-around, space-evenly (and stretch only where valid).
- `align-items`: normal, stretch, center, start, end, self-start, self-end, flex-start, flex-end, baseline, first baseline, last baseline.
- `align-content`: normal, start, end, center, stretch, space-between, space-around, space-evenly, flex-start, flex-end, baseline where supported.
- `flex-direction`: row, row-reverse, column, column-reverse.
- `flex-wrap`: nowrap, wrap, wrap-reverse.

Explain Main Axis and Cross Axis, and update the helper when Direction changes.

### 4.3 Flex Item Alignment

| UI control | CSS mapping | Values |
|---|---|---|
| Align Self | `align-self` | auto, normal, stretch, center, start, end, self-start, self-end, flex-start, flex-end, baseline |
| Order | `order` | integer |
| Flex Grow | `flex-grow` | non-negative number |
| Flex Shrink | `flex-shrink` | non-negative number |
| Flex Basis | `flex-basis` | auto, content, length, percentage |
| Flex shorthand | `flex` | validated shorthand/presets |

Do not expose a misleading Flex `Justify Self` control: it does not align Flex items in the same way as Grid item self-alignment.

### 4.4 Grid Container Alignment

| UI control | CSS mapping | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Justify Items | `justify-items` | Inline-axis alignment inside grid cells |
| Align Items | `align-items` | Block-axis alignment inside grid cells |
| Place Items | `place-items` | align-items + justify-items shorthand |
| Justify Content | `justify-content` | Grid tracks along inline axis |
| Align Content | `align-content` | Grid tracks along block axis |
| Place Content | `place-content` | align-content + justify-content shorthand |
| Gap / Row Gap / Column Gap | `gap`, `row-gap`, `column-gap` | Track spacing |

Grid-specific controls:
- `grid-template-columns`, `grid-template-rows`, `grid-template-areas`.
- `grid-auto-flow`, `grid-auto-columns`, `grid-auto-rows`.
- `grid-column`, `grid-row`, `grid-column-start/end`, `grid-row-start/end`.
- Item `justify-self`, `align-self`, `place-self`.

Provide a practical track editor supporting fixed, fractional (`fr`), `repeat()`, and `minmax()` values where feasible, plus raw CSS value mode. Do not limit users to a fixed number of columns.

### 4.5 Block / Normal Flow Alignment

Do not imply that `justify-content` or `align-items` controls ordinary block children. Provide applicable controls such as:
- Width/max-width and `margin-inline: auto` for common centered containers.
- Text alignment for text.
- Convert container to Flex or Grid to align child elements as a group.
- Positioning only when intentionally selected.

Show a hint: “To align child elements as a group, change Display to Flex or Grid.”

### 4.6 Alignment UX

- Show visual diagrams for Flex main/cross axes and Grid cell alignment.
- Label controls with user-facing names and CSS property hints where useful.
- Provide start/center/end/stretch/baseline presets.
- Keep raw value entry for valid advanced values.
- Hide or disable inapplicable controls with an explanation; never silently accept a no-op.
- Reset individual properties and the Alignment group.
- Support logical `start`/`end` values and document browser compatibility.

