## 6. Sizing

Support:
- Width, height, min-width, min-height, max-width, max-height.
- Aspect ratio.
- Logical inline-size/block-size and min/max equivalents in Advanced.
- Fit presets: auto, min-content, max-content, fit-content, stretch where valid.
- Units: px, %, rem, em, vw, vh, svw, svh, lvh, dvh, ch; `fr` only in relevant Grid fields.
- CSS expressions: `calc()`, `min()`, `max()`, `clamp()`.

Provide numeric input plus unit selector, valid raw CSS entry, Auto/Fit/Fill presets where appropriate, and distinguish authored from computed values where feasible.

## 7. Spacing

Support:
- Margin and padding for all four sides.
- Margin/padding shorthand.
- Logical margin/padding inline and block properties.
- Gap, row-gap, column-gap.
- Auto margins.
- Negative margins where valid; never negative padding.
- Linked/unlinked side controls.

Provide a Box Model visual editor showing Content, Padding, Border, and Margin. Clicking a side focuses its input. Support units and CSS expressions.

## 8. Typography

Support:
- `font-family`, `font-size`, `font-weight`, `font-style`, `font-stretch`.
- `line-height`, `letter-spacing`, `word-spacing`.
- `text-align`, `text-align-last`, `text-indent`, `text-transform`.
- `text-decoration-line/style/color/thickness`, `text-underline-offset`.
- `text-shadow`, `white-space`, `overflow-wrap`, `word-break`, `hyphens`.
- `line-clamp` where supported.
- `direction`, `writing-mode` in Advanced.
- `color`, `vertical-align` in applicable contexts.

Integrate active site theme typography tokens. Distinguish Theme Token, inherited value, and local override. Provide Reset to Theme Token.

## 9. Background

Support:
- Background color and image.
- Multiple background layers where supported.
- Image position, size (auto/cover/contain/custom), repeat, attachment (with mobile caveats), origin and clip.
- Background blend mode.
- Linear, radial, and conic gradients with editable color stops.
- Overlay convenience controls only if they compile to inspectable CSS or a documented generated pseudo-element.

Asset selection uses the user's approved media storage workflow. Do not expose private Drive IDs in public output.

## 10. Border and Outline

Support:
- Border side width/style/color and shorthand.
- Border radius per corner and linked radius.
- Logical border properties in Advanced.
- Outline width/style/color/offset.
- Divider styling for applicable elements.
- `border-image` in Advanced if supported.

Provide common presets but preserve arbitrary valid values.

## 11. Effects and Filters

Support:
- Box shadow with multiple layers.
- Text shadow.
- Opacity.
- Filters: blur, brightness, contrast, grayscale, hue-rotate, invert, saturate, sepia, drop-shadow.
- Backdrop filter where supported.
- Mix-blend-mode, background-blend-mode, isolation.
- Clip-path presets and raw CSS value mode.
- Mask properties in Advanced if supported.

Warn about expensive filters, especially on mobile.

## 12. Overflow and Scroll

Support:
- `overflow`, `overflow-x`, `overflow-y`: visible, hidden, clip, scroll, auto.
- `overscroll-behavior`, `scroll-behavior`.
- `scroll-snap-type`, `scroll-snap-align`, `scroll-snap-stop` in Advanced.
- `resize` for applicable elements.
- `object-fit`, `object-position` for image/video.
- `aspect-ratio` for media sizing.

Distinguish clipping from scrolling in UI copy.

## 13. Positioning and Stacking

Support:
- `position`: static, relative, absolute, fixed, sticky.
- Top/right/bottom/left and inset shorthand.
- Logical inset properties in Advanced.
- `z-index`.
- Isolation/stacking-context guidance.
- Sticky offsets.
- Anchor positioning only after browser and engine support validation.

Show a visual offset editor. Explain that Absolute positioning is relative to the nearest positioned ancestor and can affect responsiveness. Do not silently set a parent to relative without informing the user.

## 14. Transform

Support:
- Translate X/Y/Z.
- Rotate.
- Scale X/Y.
- Skew X/Y.
- Transform origin.
- Transform box where supported.
- 2D/3D mode and perspective in Advanced.

Use visual controls plus numeric inputs. Preserve raw transform values when loading external documents.

## 15. Transition and Animation

### Transition
Support transition property, duration, delay, timing-function presets, custom cubic-bezier, and multiple declarations where practical.

### Animation
Support animation name/keyframe selection, duration, delay, timing function, iteration count, direction, fill mode, play state, and reduced-motion behavior.

Provide a keyframe editor only if keyframes can be persisted and compiled reliably. Otherwise support CSS keyframes through Advanced Custom CSS and label the limitation. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; do not animate essential content by default.

## 16. Responsive Property Model

Use the project's canonical breakpoint definitions. At minimum support Desktop, Tablet, and Mobile. Custom breakpoints may be added only when style schema, preview, and publishing compiler support them consistently.

Recommended cascade:
1. Base/Desktop authored value.
2. Tablet override when defined.
3. Mobile override when defined.
4. Browser default when no authored or inherited value applies.

Document the exact media-query strategy. For each property:
- Show inherited versus explicit override.
- Provide Reset to Inherited, Copy from Breakpoint, and Clear Override.
- Switching device preview must not create an override.
- Keep authored values distinct from computed browser values.

Responsive editing must cover Layout, Flex/Grid, Alignment, Sizing, Spacing, Typography, Background positioning, Positioning/Visibility where supported, Order, and Grid placement.

Device preview is viewport simulation, not a separate page or element copy.

## 17. Theme Tokens and Cascade

Support Global Theme Tokens, shared component styles, element overrides, and responsive overrides.

Recommended precedence:
1. Element breakpoint override.
2. Element base override.
3. Component style.
4. Site theme token/style.
5. Builder/browser default.

Generated CSS must match this model without accidental specificity escalation.

For token-backed values:
- Display token name and resolved value.
- Allow detach/local override.
- Provide Reset to Theme Token.
- Theme changes update linked elements.
- Local overrides remain until reset.

## 18. Custom CSS and Advanced Values

Custom CSS scopes:
- Element.
- Page.
- Site/global.

Requirements:
- Scope is visible and explicit.
- Validate syntax where practical; show diagnostics.
- Do not silently discard unsupported rules.
- Prevent leakage into IndyShares admin/editor UI.
- Scope published output to the user's public site.
- Preserve unknown declarations through load/save.
- Never expose Google tokens or platform secrets to custom code.

Raw values should support valid `calc()`, `min()`, `max()`, `clamp()`, `var(--token)`, Grid `minmax()`/`repeat()`, and modern color functions where browser support is acceptable. `!important` belongs only in an explicit advanced workflow with a warning.

Do not parse valid CSS into a lossy simplified representation. Preserve values the visual editor cannot fully interpret and offer raw-value fallback.

## 19. Pseudo-States and Selectors

Where supported, provide Default, Hover, Focus, Focus-visible, Active, Visited (applicable links), and Disabled (applicable controls).

Clearly show the state being edited. Editor selection/hover outlines must not be confused with published hover styles. Focus styling must remain accessible. Scope state CSS to the selected element/component. Pseudo-elements (`::before`, `::after`) may be supported in Advanced only if persistence and rendering are reliable.

## 20. Property Applicability Rules

The Property Editor must understand selected element type, parent display mode, container/item role, element category, breakpoint, theme-token linkage, and pseudo-state.

Examples:
- Flex container: Direction, Wrap, Justify Content, Align Items, Align Content, Gap.
- Flex child: Align Self, Order, Grow, Shrink, Basis.
- Grid container: tracks, auto flow, container alignment, gaps.
- Grid child: row/column placement and self-alignment.
- Image: Object Fit and Object Position.
- Text: typography and text alignment.
- Normal block: no misleading Flex/Grid controls until Display changes.

If unsupported by the selected engine/element, explain why and preserve existing CSS when possible.

