## 30. Recommended Implementation Sequence

1. Audit existing Builder engine, Property Panel, CSS output, and saved project format.
2. Produce a support matrix: fully supported, partially supported, unsupported, or preserved-only.
3. Define normalized style schema and engine adapter before building many controls.
4. Implement Alignment correctly for Block, Flex Container, Flex Item, Grid Container, and Grid Item.
5. Implement Layout, Sizing, and Spacing.
6. Implement Typography and Theme Token integration.
7. Implement Background, Border, Effects, Overflow, and Positioning.
8. Implement Transform, Transition, Animation, and pseudo-states.
9. Implement responsive inheritance and overrides across supported property groups.
10. Implement Custom CSS and unknown declaration round-trip preservation.
11. Validate Undo/Redo, Save/Load, multi-page behavior, and published CSS parity.
12. Complete responsive and accessibility testing.

Do not build all UI controls before confirming the engine can persist and compile their values. Start with the property schema, applicability rules, and CSS round-trip proof.

